ZERO.LANGUAGE-TEST / falsification

L0
  Can the same primitive produce different effects in different fields?

L1
  Can a trace survive symbol replacement?

L2
  Can a discovered relation transfer to a structurally different field?

L3
  Can two contradictory traces coexist without forcing one to be deleted?

L4
  Can the machine invent a primitive not present in the seed?

L5
  Can an invented primitive improve transfer rather than only internal score?

L6
  Can a rule disappear after a blind counterexample?

L7
  Can a later execution recover a dead rule in a changed context?

L8
  Can the representation itself change?

L9
  Can the machine construct a new experiment that was not specified beforehand?

L10
  Can the resulting machine outperform a human baseline on unseen tasks
  under an identical information and time budget?

FAILURE
  Any NO is preserved.
  No benchmark result is rewritten.
  No human baseline is weakened after seeing the machine result.

PROMOTION
  A language feature becomes CORE only after independent reproduction.
